# ale-furtado.netlify.app served a complete, crawlable copy of this site. Confirmed
# 21 August 2026, AFTER alefurtado.org was already set as the primary domain in the
# Netlify UI: the subdomain still returned 200 with no Location header. **Setting the
# primary domain does NOT redirect Netlify's own subdomain**, whatever earlier notes
# and the audit assumed. This rule is the only thing that does it.
#
# The `from` is an absolute URL, so it matches ONE host. Branch previews live on
# <branch>--ale-furtado.netlify.app and cannot match it, which is what makes this safe
# where a looser pattern would have taken the v2 preview down. alefurtado.org cannot
# match it either, so there is no redirect loop.
#
# The `!` is required. Without the force flag Netlify serves the matching file first and
# the rule never fires, which is exactly why the subdomain was returning 200.
#
# Must stay at the TOP: Netlify takes the first matching rule.
http://ale-furtado.netlify.app/*   https://alefurtado.org/:splat  301!
https://ale-furtado.netlify.app/*  https://alefurtado.org/:splat  301!

/card      /card.html      200
/method    /method.html    200
/services  /services.html  200
/product-sheet    /assets/delivery-readiness-review.pdf    200
# The canonical page. Netlify would resolve this on its own, and the rule is here for the
# same reason /card and /method carry one: the behaviour is implicit and this makes it not.
/monday-morning-test    /monday-morning-test.html    200
# The short spoken alias. A 301 rather than a 200, so the analytics stay on one URL.
/monday    /monday-morning-test    301
